<title>ESTONIA: PENNU, WESTERN AGREE ON FACTORY LAUNCH.</title>
<headline>PENNU, WESTERN AGREE ON FACTORY LAUNCH.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennu Computer said on Wednesday that Western Digital Corporation had in principle decided to start cooperating in the launch of hard disk drive factory.</p>
<p>&quot;Western will bring the equipment and give training while Pennu will take care of premises,&quot; director Lembit Abileid told Reuters.</p>
<p>The timing schedule of a new factory, which will get investments of about six million kroons, will be fixed in July, Abileid added.  </p>
<p>Pennu had said earlier that it plans to supply the Baltic, Nordic countries and eastern Europe with a handling capacity of 1,000 hard disks per months.</p>
<p>Later, capacity may grow to 4,000-5,000 disks per months.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
